# GMP access safety rules

Apply these rules when the user asks to add, remove, inspect, or change a person's
Google Analytics, GTM, Search Console / SC / GSC, AdWords, or Google Ads access,
including 入职、离职、升职、负责新项目.

1. Use only the local gmp executable, sibling-project CLIs, and official public
   Google APIs. Never use Browser, Chrome, Playwright, DOM extraction, browser
   cookies/tokens, or private web endpoints.
2. Run gmp doctor before promising a write, and gmp catalog when brand or
   resource IDs are uncertain. Doctor also reports the auxiliary gmp_org
   surface. Use gmp discover --product gmp-org only for official organization
   and Analytics account-link reads. Read access never proves manage.users.
3. Mutations never execute directly. grant, revoke, set-role, onboard, offboard,
   promote, and mutation task must create an immutable plan_id. Show email,
   operation, products, roles, resource IDs, blockers, and manual items. After
   explicit user confirmation, execute exactly:
   gmp apply PLAN_ID --confirm PLAN_ID.
4. Raw mutation --execute is forbidden. Plans are bound to the catalog SHA-256;
   a catalog change invalidates an older plan. Plans are single-use once a
   remote execution attempt starts. Never replay a failed, partial, or unknown
   plan; read current state and create a new plan.
5. grant / onboard / promote only add or raise access; never downgrade.
   set-role is an exact replacement and requires one product plus one role.
   revoke affects only named targets. offboard accepts no brand/product scope,
   uses account-wide GA/GTM revocation, all cataloged Ads customers plus MCC,
   and all known GSC sites. Account-wide actions can affect resources not listed
   individually in catalog. Reconcile live GA/GTM account boundaries, GSC sites,
   and the Ads MCC customer tree before plan creation and again under the apply
   lock before claim/audit/write. Any read error or two-way catalog drift fails
   closed without consuming the plan.
6. GA/GTM/Ads Admin plans require explicit --allow-admin both when planning and
   applying. GSC Owner is always blocked by this CLI. The flag does not bypass
   Google authorization or provider limits.
7. GSC Full/Restricted user ACL has no official public API. Keep each GSC action
   in the unified plan with method=manual; apply must return manual_required,
   never success. Do not substitute Site Verification Owner, a users URL, or
   browser automation as an executed result.
8. Ads invitations are pending_acceptance until the recipient accepts the
   email. Do not report them as fully provisioned.
9. Cross-product execution is not transactional. After apply, run gmp history
   and report every product/resource as ok, skipped, pending_acceptance,
   manual_required, blocked, partial, unknown, or error. Top-level ok excludes
   blocked/partial/unknown/error; complete requires every item to be ok/skipped.
   Never turn partial or unknown execution into “all successful.”
   Apply exits 0 only when complete, 2 when follow-up remains, and 1 on failure;
   callers must also inspect ok, complete, and requires_follow_up.
10. Reference credentials/resources from ../GA MCP, ../GTM MCP, ../SEO-Agent,
    and ../Adwords API; never copy or print secrets.
11. Files under scripts/ and ops/ are historical evidence, not supported
    execution paths.
12. The user's 2026-09-02 screenshot is manual evidence that
    YOUR_GMP_SA@YOUR_GCP_PROJECT.iam.gserviceaccount.com has direct Org Admin, User
    Admin, and Billing Admin roles in Your Organization. Treat those as real
    organization roles, but never claim the public API verified them.
13. The public GMP Admin API v1alpha has no users, memberships, roles, or
    permissions endpoint. Its current disabled state affects organization and
    Analytics account-link discovery only; enabling it would not create an
    organization personnel ACL. Employee changes still use GA/GTM/Ads product
    APIs, while GSC remains manual_required.
14. write_candidate/write_unverified is evidence for a guarded product-API
    attempt, not verified write authority or proof that a change occurred.
15. Answer in Chinese unless the user asks otherwise.
